  "title": "High-Risk AI Impact Assessment",
  "content": "Deployers would have been required to complete an impact assessment for each covered high-risk artificial intelligence system, repeat it at least annually and after intentional and substantial modifications, and retain the assessment records. The obligation was enacted in Colorado SB 24-205 but never became operative because the statute was superseded before its delayed effective date.",
